<title>UK: Bass shares fall, talk of stock overhang.</title>
<headline>Bass shares fall, talk of stock overhang.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Bass Plc slipped in thin trade on Friday amid talk of a stock overhang in the market and hedging activity in Bass futures, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;Someone has been left with stock on their hands and is attempting to hedge his position in the futures,&quot; one senior trader said.</p>
<p>The shares were down 10p at 755-1/2p by 0930 GMT as nervous investors awaited the OFT report on the company's planned Carlsberg-Tetley brewing purchase.</p>
<p>-- Elaine Hardcastle, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4027</p>
